-- title:
--   The shared candidate history of one level
-- statement:
--   These notions belong to a proof that every reflexive real Banach space has the fixed point property for nonexpansive maps: every $F:C\to C$ with $\|Fa-Fb\|\le\|a-b\|$ on a nonempty closed bounded convex set $C$ has a fixed point. The proof assumes a fixed-point-free map, reduces to a minimal invariant set $K$ of diameter $1$, builds an adaptive weighted tree of nonexpansive maps generated by resolvents, and contradicts the minimality through detecting functionals. The tree is built level by level from candidate records: each candidate is a generated map attached to a parent node together with a norm-one functional chosen after the map, and every candidate, including those that later receive coefficient zero, consumes a global ordinal $n$ with budget $2^{-(n+9)}$. Fix a stage of the construction and its level recursion over parents.
--
--   1. **Stage returns and records.** The parent return processed at step $n$ and its list of records, including discarded ones. The number of records chosen for parent $p$ is $N_p$.
--   2. **Shared history.** Each step appends its records, so the history before parent $p$ has length $\sum_{q<p}N_q$. The final history consists of exactly all groups, of total length $\sum_pN_p$.
--   3. **Level record.** The record at a global ordinal, decoded through the group concatenation. It is legal relative to the exact prefix of the final history before it:
--   $$
--   \mathrm{Legal}\bigl(\text{history}_{<i},\ \mathrm{record}_i\bigr).
--   $$
